title CampusClaw Optional Credential Forwarding (Pending implementation)

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 21c3f59be033e7bdd5506a2d9d48baa2581bc3c7):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/
' RuntimeEventController.java: submit; RuntimeRequestContext.java: mateCredentials.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/
' HttpMateToolClient.java: invokeTool, queryToolIdsByAgentId, queryToolIdsBySkillId, queryToolMetaByIds.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/dto/RequestHeaderInfo.java: toHeaders.
' Observed behavior: four headers are captured; RuntimeEventService.requireCredentials still rejects incomplete values.
' Pending implementation: remove local checks in the entry, CallMateTool.execute, and HttpMateToolClient.invokeTool.
' Product constraint: context headers are optional; POST Events and Command may include access-token.
' Security hardening: keep received values only in one execution snapshot and never persist or log them.
' Security boundary: discovery, model, and other calls are credential-free; only Mate execute forwards
' the received X-HW-ID, Authorization, X-HW-APPKEY, and access-token values without renaming.


actor "mate-service" as Caller
participant "Runtime Controller" as Controller
participant "Runtime Service" as Service
participant "Model Manager" as Model
participant "Mate Tool API" as Mate

== Freeze operation context ==
alt POST Events or Command
  Caller -> Controller : optional context headers\nand optional access-token
  Controller -> Controller : bind inputs and create immutable snapshot\nempty or partial values are allowed
else any other Runtime operation
  Caller -> Controller : operation-specific headers\ncreateSession: optional Accept-Language only
  Controller -> Controller : bind operation inputs\nwithout credential validation
end
== Route downstream calls ==
Controller -> Service : execute operation with scoped context
Service -> Model : model request\nno execution credential headers
Service -> Mate : Agent, Skill, or metadata discovery\nno execution credential headers
opt actual Mate tool execution
  Service -> Mate : POST tool execute, even with an empty snapshot\nforward provided non-empty values only
  Mate --> Service : validate credentials; success or failure\nClaw maps failure to isError=true
end
== Complete and release ==
Service --> Controller : operation result or SSE publisher
Controller --> Caller : normal HTTP, SSE, or business error response

note over Caller,Controller
  Upstream verifies credential authenticity and action
  authorization. Runtime does not check completeness,
  mutual exclusion, Bearer shape, or whether
  Authorization and X-HW-APPKEY are both present.
end note

note over Controller,Service
  Header names are case-insensitive under HTTP. The
  contract preserves the exact access-token spelling.
  Credential values remain opaque and are never
  logged, persisted, copied into ResultBean, Prompt,
  or Event, or used as Session ownership. The snapshot
  is discarded when the execution ends. Runtime
  declares no local authentication error codes.
end note
@enduml
